{"id":"mahabharata-12-032","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":32,"title":"द्वात्रिंशत्तमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 32 · Vyasa on atonement","summary":{"en":"Vyasa tells Yudhishthira that he must not give up sorrow for the dead by dying, and that, while alive, he must perform the expiation for the sin of the war. Yudhishthira says that he does not doubt Vyasa's word, but is held back by shame.","kn":"ಸತ್ತವರ ದುಃಖಕ್ಕೆ ಪ್ರಾಣ ಬಿಡಬಾರದು, ಜೀವಂತವಾಗಿದ್ದು ಯುದ್ಧ ಪಾಪಕ್ಕೆ ಪ್ರಾಯಶ್ಚಿತ್ತ ಮಾಡಬೇಕೆಂದು ವ್ಯಾಸರು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ವ್ಯಾಸರ ಮಾತನ್ನು ಸಂಶಯಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲ, ಆದರೆ ನಾಚಿಕೆ ತಡೆಯುತ್ತದೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"व्यास युधिष्ठिर से कहते हैं कि मृतकों के शोक में प्राण नहीं देने चाहिए, जीवित रहकर युद्ध के पाप का प्रायश्चित्त करना चाहिए। युधिष्ठिर कहते हैं कि वे व्यास की बात पर संशय नहीं करते, पर लज्जा उन्हें रोकती है।","te":"చనిపోయినవారి దుఃఖంతో ప్రాణం విడవకూడదని, బతికి ఉండి యుద్ధ పాపానికి ప్రాయశ్చిత్తం చేయాలని వ్యాసుడు యుధిష్ఠిరునికి చెబుతాడు. వ్యాసుని మాటను సందేహించనని, కానీ సిగ్గు ఆపుతుందని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అంటాడు.","ta":"இறந்தவருக்காக உயிர் விடக்கூடாது, உயிருடன் இருந்து போரின் பாவத்துக்குப் பிராயச்சித்தம் செய்ய வேண்டும் என்று வியாசர் யுதிஷ்டிரரிடம் கூறுகிறார். வியாசரின் சொல்லை ஐயுறவில்லை, ஆனால் நாணம் தடுக்கிறது என்கிறார் யுதிஷ்டிரர்.","ml":"മരിച്ചവരെയോർത്ത് മരണത്താൽ ദുഃഖം ഉപേക്ഷിക്കരുതെന്നും, ജീവിച്ചിരിക്കുമ്പോൾ യുദ്ധത്തിന്റെ പാപത്തിനുള്ള പ്രായശ്ചിത്തം ചെയ്യണമെന്നും വ്യാസൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനോട് പറയുന്നു. വ്യാസന്റെ വാക്കിൽ താൻ സംശയിക്കുന്നില്ലെന്നും, എന്നാൽ ലജ്ജ തന്നെ പിടിച്ചുനിർത്തുന്നുവെന്നും യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ മറുപടി പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.32; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"तूष्णींभूतं तु राजानं शोचमानं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nतपस्वी धर्मतत्त्वज्ञः कृष्णद्वैपायनोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"To King Yudhishthira, silent and grieving, the ascetic Krishna Dvaipayana, who knew the truth of dharma, spoke."}},{"n":2,"text":"प्रजानां पालनं धर्मो राज्ञां राजीवलोचन ।\nधर्मः प्रमाणं लोकस्य नित्यं धर्मानुवर्तनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lotus-eyed one, the dharma of kings is to protect their subjects; dharma is the authority for the world, and following it is a constant duty."}},{"n":3,"text":"अनुतिष्ठस्व वै राजन्पितृपैतामहं पदम् ।\nब्राह्मणेषु च यो धर्मः स नित्यो वेदनिश्चितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, follow the path of your father and grandfather; the dharma that belongs to brahmins is eternal and settled by the Veda."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्प्रमाणं प्रमाणानां शाश्वतं भरतर्षभ ।\nतस्य धर्मस्य कृत्स्नस्य क्षत्रियः परिरक्षिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bull of the Bharatas, that is the standard of all standards and everlasting; the kshatriya is the protector of that dharma in its entirety."}},{"n":5,"text":"तथा यः प्रतिहन्त्यस्य शासनं विषये नरः ।\nस बाहुभ्यां विनिग्राह्यो लोकयात्राविघातकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man in the realm who obstructs the king's command, wrecking the order of the world, must be restrained by force of arms."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रमाणमप्रमाणं यः कुर्यान्मोहवशं गतः ।\nभृत्यो वा यदि वा पुत्रस्तपस्वी वापि कश्चन ।\nपापान्सर्वैरुपायैस्तान्नियच्छेद्घातयेत वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anyone, servant, son or ascetic, who in delusion turns the authoritative into the unauthoritative, those sinners the king should restrain or have killed by every means."}},{"n":7,"text":"अतोऽन्यथा वर्तमानो राजा प्राप्नोति किल्बिषम् ।\nधर्मं विनश्यमानं हि यो न रक्षेत्स धर्महा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who acts otherwise incurs guilt; whoever does not protect dharma when it is being destroyed is a destroyer of dharma."}},{"n":8,"text":"ते त्वया धर्महन्तारो निहताः सपदानुगाः ।\nस्वधर्मे वर्तमानस्त्वं किं नु शोचसि पाण्डव ।\nराजा हि हन्याद्दद्याच्च प्रजा रक्षेच्च धर्मतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have killed those destroyers of dharma with their followers. Why do you grieve, son of Pandu, when you acted in your own dharma? A king should slay and give and protect his subjects according to dharma."}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":9,"text":"न तेऽभिशङ्के वचनं यद्ब्रवीषि तपोधन ।\nअपरोक्षो हि ते धर्मः सर्वधर्मभृतां वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not doubt your words, ascetic, for dharma is plain to you, best of those who uphold all dharma."}},{"n":10,"text":"मया ह्यवध्या बहवो घातिता राज्यकारणात् ।\nतान्यकार्याणि मे ब्रह्मन्दहन्ति च तपन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I caused many who should not have been killed to be killed for the sake of a kingdom; those wrongs burn and torment me, brahmin."}},{"text":"व्यास उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vyasa said:"}},{"n":11,"text":"ईश्वरो वा भवेत्कर्ता पुरुषो वापि भारत ।\nहठो वा वर्तते लोके कर्मजं वा फलं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether God is the doer, or man, or chance rules in the world, or the fruit is said to arise from action, consider this."}},{"n":12,"text":"ईश्वरेण नियुक्ता हि साध्वसाधु च पार्थिव ।\nकुर्वन्ति पुरुषाः कर्म फलमीश्वरगामि तत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men do good and bad deeds as directed by God, king; the fruit of the deed goes to God."}},{"n":13,"text":"यथा हि पुरुषश्छिन्द्याद्वृक्षं परशुना वने ।\nछेत्तुरेव भवेत्पापं परशोर्न कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just as a man who cuts a tree in the forest with an axe, the sin would be the cutter's alone and in no way the axe's."}},{"n":14,"text":"अथ वा तदुपादानात्प्राप्नुयुः कर्मणः फलम् ।\nदण्डशस्त्रकृतं पापं पुरुषे तन्न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or, if people took the fruit of an act because they were its instrument, then sin done with rod and weapon would not be found in the man."}},{"n":15,"text":"न चैतदिष्टं कौन्तेय यदन्येन फलं कृतम् ।\nप्राप्नुयादिति तस्माच्च ईश्वरे तन्निवेशय ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kunti's son, it is not accepted that another should take the fruit of what someone else has done; so place it on God."}},{"n":16,"text":"अथ वा पुरुषः कर्ता कर्मणोः शुभपापयोः ।\nन परं विद्यते तस्मादेवमन्यच्छुभं कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if man is the doer of good and bad deeds, there is nothing higher than him; so do some other good instead."}},{"n":17,"text":"न हि कश्चित्क्वचिद्राजन्दिष्टात्प्रतिनिवर्तते ।\nदण्डशस्त्रकृतं पापं पुरुषे तन्न विद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"No one, O king, ever turns back from what is fated; so sin done with rod and weapon is not found in the man."}},{"n":18,"text":"यदि वा मन्यसे राजन्हठे लोकं प्रतिष्ठितम् ।\nएवमप्यशुभं कर्म न भूतं न भविष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you hold that the world rests on chance, even so no evil deed has ever been or will be."}},{"n":19,"text":"अथाभिपत्तिर्लोकस्य कर्तव्या शुभपापयोः ।\nअभिपन्नतमं लोके राज्ञामुद्यतदण्डनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And if one must adopt some view of good and evil, the most accepted in the world is that kings raise the rod of punishment."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथापि लोके कर्माणि समावर्तन्त भारत ।\nशुभाशुभफलं चेमे प्राप्नुवन्तीति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if actions merely keep revolving in the world and creatures receive good and bad results, that is my view too."}},{"n":21,"text":"एवं सत्यं शुभादेशं कर्मणस्तत्फलं ध्रुवम् ।\nत्यज तद्राजशार्दूल मैवं शोके मनः कृथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So it is true that what is good is prescribed and the fruit of the act is certain; give up that grief, tiger among kings, and do not set your mind on sorrow."}},{"n":22,"text":"स्वधर्मे वर्तमानस्य सापवादेऽपि भारत ।\nएवमात्मपरित्यागस्तव राजन्न शोभनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who acts in his own dharma, even if blamed, Bharata, such abandoning of yourself does not suit you, king."}},{"n":23,"text":"विहितानीह कौन्तेय प्रायश्चित्तानि कर्मिणाम् ।\nशरीरवांस्तानि कुर्यादशरीरः पराभवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Atonements for those who act have been laid down here, son of Kunti; one with a body can perform them, one without a body is defeated."}},{"n":24,"text":"तद्राजञ्जीवमानस्त्वं प्रायश्चित्तं चरिष्यसि ।\nप्रायश्चित्तमकृत्वा तु प्रेत्य तप्तासि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, king, while alive you will perform atonement; but without atonement, Bharata, you would suffer after death."}}]}]}